meta {
  name: Biovega Services Catalog
}

auth {
  mode: oauth2
}

auth:oauth2 {
  grant_type: authorization_code
  callback_url: 
  authorization_url: 
  access_token_url: 
  refresh_token_url: 
  client_id: 
  client_secret: 
  scope: 
  state: 
  pkce: false
  credentials_placement: body
  credentials_id: credentials
  token_placement: header
  token_header_prefix: Bearer
  auto_fetch_token: true
  auto_refresh_token: false
}

docs {
  Biovega Services Catalog API — contract prefix /odata/v1 (the unversioned
  /odata prefix still answers but carries Deprecation headers).

  RUN ORDER for a full walkthrough: Get Token → lookups (Get Address Types,
  Get Payment Methods, Get Discount Types, Get Carriers, Get Customer
  Statuses) → Save Customer → Save Customer Address / Card → Save Order All
  → Get Order → Change Order Status → Earn / Redeem Points.

  Every tenant-scoped request needs ?companyId={{companyId}}; a missing or
  foreign companyId returns 404 (never 403). Errors on /odata/v1 come back
  as {"error":{"code","message"}}. Ids from lookups differ per environment
  — the post-response scripts capture them into env variables.

  Field-by-field mapping from the legacy ERP XML: docs/erp-to-api-mapping.html
  (English) and docs/erp-to-api-mapping-hr.html (hrvatski) in the
  biovega-services-tools repository.
}
